[[bm25-ranking]]
BM25 lexical ranking

BM25 is a bag-of-words ranking function that scores a document by how often the
query terms appear in it, discounted by how common those terms are across the whole
collection and adjusted for document length. A long document does not win simply by
repeating a word; the length normalization term keeps short and long passages on a
fair footing.

Lexical ranking shines on exact symbol names, error strings, configuration keys, and
numeric constants — the tokens that carry little semantic meaning but must match
character for character. It is also fully deterministic and explainable: you can
point at the term frequencies and inverse document frequencies that produced a score.
That transparency is why keyword ranking remains a first-class retriever even where
vector search is available.
